@title Lesson walk: heat-and-sizing says what the preview shows (hottest place, total loss)
@area Learn
# After the Do it for me and Next clicks the card shows the step that says the hottest place is -T1 (a ticked step auto-advances, so a further Next would skip it).
# The lesson says "The hottest place sits on the transformer -T1" and quotes "Total loss 34 W". The scene dump reports what the Heat view draws (the badges and the first hot-spot card), so the walk checks the words against the values at both sizes. Do it for me only carries out commands.
key ctrl+k
wait 4
text where it gets hot
wait 6
click_text "Where it gets hot, and how big the cabinet must be"
wait 40
shot 01-open-cabinet
check_layout
try click_text "Do it for me"
wait 40
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
shot 02-heat-on-step
check_layout
try click_text "Do it for me"
wait 40
try click_text "Next"
wait 20
shot 03-hottest-place
expect "Total loss 34 W"
expect "Preview, not a solver result"
expect_scene "heat preview: hottest =A1+CAB-T1 first card =A1+CAB-T1 total 34 W"
expect "The hottest place sits on the transformer"
check_layout
